{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412356","formula":"SiC","hill":"CSi","elements":["C","Si"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"Si":1.0},"names":{"en":"Silicon carbide","ru":"Карбид кремния","uk":"Карбід кремнію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Silicon carbide (SiC), also known as carborundum (), is a hard chemical compound of silicon and carbon. A wide bandgap semiconductor, it occurs in nature as the extremely rare mineral moissanite, but has been mass-produced as powder and crystals since 1893 for use as an abrasive. Grains of silicon carbide can be bonded together by sintering to form very hard ceramics that are widely used in applications requiring high endurance, such as disc brakes, clutches and ballistic plates in bulletproof vests.","ru":"Карби́д кре́мния (карбору́нд) — бинарное неорганическое химическое соединение кремния с углеродом. Химическая формула SiC. В природе встречается в виде чрезвычайно редкого минерала — муассанита. Порошок карбида кремния был получен в 1893 году.","uk":"Карбі́д кре́мнію, також карбору́нд — бінарна неорганічна сполука кремнію з вуглецем."},"fame":54,"pubchemCid":9863,"mass":40.096,"charge":0,"smiles":"[C-]#[Si+]","inchikey":"HBMJWWWQQXIZIP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methanidylidynesilanylium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-7140","atoms":20,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.074,0.0,0.0],[-1.537,2.662,0.0],[0.0,0.0,5.045]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":1.774,"z":2.521,"el":"Si"},{"x":1.537,"y":0.887,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":1.537,"y":0.887,"z":5.045,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.774,"z":4.417,"el":"C"},{"x":1.537,"y":0.887,"z":1.894,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.537,"y":4.436,"z":2.521,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.549,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.549,"z":5.045,"el":"Si"},{"x":-1.537,"y":4.436,"z":4.417,"el":"C"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.549,"z":1.894,"el":"C"},{"x